From 37a41b1260b364c7ddea96b29641dc4ee6f8e3a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iuri Jikidze <37273763+ijiki16@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:14:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/39] pinctrl: sunxi: use 2-bit power mode fields on A733
 (NCAT3)

On the A733, GPIO_POW_MOD_SEL (PIO + 0x40) holds a 2-bit field per
bank, bits [2n+1:2n] for bank n (A733 User Manual V0.92, 18.14):
00/10 = 3.3 V withstand mode, 01 = auto, 11 = 1.8 V. The fields reset to
10 (3.3 V); boot0 on the OrangePi 4 Pro sets most banks to 01 (auto).

sunxi_pinctrl_set_io_bias_cfg() treats BIAS_VOLTAGE_PIO_POW_MODE_SEL as
one bit per bank with 1 = 1.8 V. On the A733 that clobbers the wrong
bits and selects 3.3 V mode for a 1.8 V bank. Write the 2-bit field
for the NCAT3 register layout instead (11 for <= 1.8 V, 10 otherwise).

This only matters once a vcc-pX-supply is described for a bank; no
upstream A733 board does that today, so there is no runtime effect yet.
Verified on an OrangePi 4 Pro by temporarily adding 1.8 V vcc-pc/vcc-ph
supplies: POW_MOD_SEL read back 0x0115d570, i.e. PC and PH = 11 and the
other banks left untouched. Not otherwise tested.

No Fixes tag: the A733 pinctrl support this corrects comes from the
mainline base of this series, whose history is not available in this
(shallow) tree.

This change was made with the help of an AI coding assistant (Claude).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.c b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.c
index 181d02959..d76666b73 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.c
@@ -785,6 +785,23 @@ static int sunxi_pinctrl_set_io_bias_cfg(struct sunxi_pinctrl *pctl,
 
 		fallthrough;
 	case BIAS_VOLTAGE_PIO_POW_MODE_SEL:
+		/*
+		 * A733 (NCAT3): GPIO_POW_MOD_SEL holds a 2-bit field per bank
+		 * (00/10: 3.3V, 01: auto, 11: 1.8V), resetting to 10 (3.3V).
+		 * A bank powered at 1.8V left at 10 cannot reliably read inputs.
+		 */
+		if (pctl->flags & SUNXI_PINCTRL_NCAT3_REG_LAYOUT) {
+			val = uV <= 1800000 ? 0x3 : 0x2;
+
+			raw_spin_lock_irqsave(&pctl->lock, flags);
+			reg = readl(pctl->membase + pctl->pow_mod_sel_offset);
+			reg &= ~(0x3 << (bank * 2));
+			writel(reg | val << (bank * 2),
+			       pctl->membase + pctl->pow_mod_sel_offset);
+			raw_spin_unlock_irqrestore(&pctl->lock, flags);
+			return 0;
+		}
+
 		val = uV <= 1800000 ? 1 : 0;
 		if (inverted)
 			val = !val;
